From: NAPI loop <noreply@local>
Date: Thu, 23 Oct 2026 16:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] configs: napi-c: run loopdetect at preboot, boot eMMC on loop

Wires the 'loopdetect' command (added by the previous patch) into the
NAPI-C boot flow via the board defconfig:

  * CONFIG_USE_PREBOOT + CONFIG_PREBOOT run 'loopdetect' before the boot
    command, setting env 'napi_loop'.
  * When napi_loop=1 (single-port loopback plug present on the onboard
    ethernet) boot_targets is reordered eMMC-first (mmc0 mmc1 ...), so the
    stock BOOTSTD 'bootflow scan' boots the eMMC OS, falling back to the SD
    (mmc1) if the eMMC is not bootable.
  * When no loopback is present boot_targets keeps its default SD-first
    order (mmc1 mmc0 ...), so the board boots whatever is on the SD card.

Detection now lives entirely in the eMMC U-Boot; the old SD-side sector-30000
NAND/PERM flag and the Linux detector service are no longer used.
---
diff --git a/configs/napi-c-rk3308_defconfig b/configs/napi-c-rk3308_defconfig
--- a/configs/napi-c-rk3308_defconfig
+++ b/configs/napi-c-rk3308_defconfig
@@ -73,3 +73,5 @@
 CONFIG_LZO=y
 CONFIG_ERRNO_STR=y
 CONFIG_CMD_NAPI_LOOPDETECT=y
+CONFIG_USE_PREBOOT=y
+CONFIG_PREBOOT="loopdetect; if test \"${napi_loop}\" = 1; then echo NAPI loopback present: booting eMMC first; setenv boot_targets \"mmc0 mmc1 nvme scsi usb pxe dhcp spi\"; fi"
